<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Yugoslav Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal Yugoslav Army was the army of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, from 1918 to 1945. Built on the Serbian army that had fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, it had a mainly Serbian officer corps. Poorly equipped and spread along long frontiers, it collapsed within days of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> invasion of April 1941 and surrendered on 17 April.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-yugoslav-army.jpg" alt="Royal Yugoslav Army" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ilustrirani Slovenec · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zastava_Triglavskog_puka.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
